r"""patch_L443_23_class_words_20261026.py -- each drawer group's JPL or IAU class name explained in
plain words, and a comet's perihelion explained in its text box, by
Tony's approval of Oct 26 ("Approved") of
documentation/WORDS_L443_glosses_20261026.md in the orrery (L-443).

Built on gallery 9223cd165422bf2616715e65ca59410b8245f9e5 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/tonyquintanilla.github.io (branch
main), AFTER patch_L443_21_comets_room_20261026.py and
patch_L443_22_atlas_gold_20261026.py have run. With orrery
5398439591f35979c4df1791e25477ac37119b01 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/palomas_orrery.

WHAT IT EDITS, all or nothing

    data/objects_config.json: the thirteen group rows of the Solar System
        room's drawer each gain an "about", the approved sentence for its
        class; the drawer's description says what it is.
    interactive.html: that sentence shows as the first bullet in the
        text box and the i panel of every body in the group; a comet's
        span sentence reads "a year before its perihelion, its closest
        point to the Sun, to a year after today"; the change note.
    tools/headless/walk_solar_system_drawer.js: West's text box and
        panel open with "Hyperbolic: ...", Sedna's with "Trans-Neptunian:
        ...", and the new span sentence.

    The groups' words reach a visitor on the push: the room reads them
    from data/objects_config.json, not from the cache. Not recorded here,
    for the records patch after the phone look: this ruling and the gold
    ruling on L-443, and the placement for interactive-exhibit's next
    version.

HOW TO RUN

    Save it in the website folder (tonyquintanilla.github.io), open it
    in VS Code and press Run, after patches 21 and 22 and before the Daily
    Run. It prints an "ok" line per file and "patch applied"; a second run
    refuses. Move it into documentation\ with patches 21 and 22 and commit
    them together. Undo before a commit is Discard Changes in GitHub
    Desktop.

Written October 26, 2026 with Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5.
"""
